3. FREE 30-DAY TRIAL

A Customer may use the complete Software free of charge for 30 consecutive
days beginning with first use of an Instance, without a credit card.
The trial includes ordinary functional use and private evaluation.

The trial is limited to one evaluation period per Customer. Reinstalling,
cloning, resetting a database, or creating replacement Instances does not
restart or extend that period. After the trial, continued use requires a
purchased license, except where separate written permission is granted.

The trial is not a transfer of ownership of the Software. The Customer
retains ownership of the data entered into or generated using the Software.

4. PAID PERPETUAL LICENSE

Following purchase and activation, the Licensor grants the Customer a
non-exclusive, non-transferable (except as required by applicable law),
perpetual right to install, run, and privately modify the licensed version
of the Software for the Customer's own purposes, including commercial
accounting and bookkeeping activity.

The advertised Core License is a one-time purchase, currently EUR 119,
subject to the price and applicable taxes displayed at checkout.
There are no recurring license fees for continued use of the purchased
version.

One Core License covers one production Instance controlled by the Customer,
with no application-imposed limits on journal entries, users, or companies
within that Instance. Reasonable test, staging, backup, and disaster-
recovery copies for the same licensed deployment are permitted. Additional
independent production Instances require separate licenses unless the
Licensor agrees otherwise in writing.

A Customer may engage an administrator or service provider to install,
operate, and maintain the licensed Instance on the Customer's behalf,
including on a VPS or server controlled or rented by the Customer.

5. UPDATES AND MAJOR UPGRADES

Security and maintenance updates for the purchased version are included
without recurring charges, consistent with the lifetime-update offer
advertised for the Core License. They do not require an annual maintenance
subscription.

New major-version upgrades may be offered as separate, optional paid
purchases. Declining a major upgrade does not terminate the Customer's
perpetual right to use the version already licensed.

Optional installation, consulting, custom development, third-party hosting,
and third-party AI/API services are not included in the Software license
unless expressly stated in a separate offer.

6. SELF-HOSTING, DATA, AND OFFLINE USE

The Software is designed to run on infrastructure controlled by the
Customer. The Licensor does not acquire ownership of the Customer's
accounting records, uploaded documents, or other Customer data.

Once successfully activated, the licensed version may continue to operate
without contacting a licensing server; the Licensor does not reserve a
